      en: ["Officially designated as a wildlife refuge on July 29, 1987.", "Protects an area of roughly 13,000 hectares of coastal wetlands.", "Famous for its population of the endangered West Indian manatee.", "Accessible only by a historic narrow-gauge train from the town of La Unión.", "Home to over 190 different bird species and various primate species.", "Located at the confluence of the Cuero and Salado rivers."],
